{
  "key": "wave",
  "meta": {
    "label": "Wave Field",
    "group": "physical",
    "thumbnail": "bi-water"
  },
  "intro": {
    "summary": "FFT-based directional ocean surface synthesis",
    "paragraphs": [
      "This app models open-ocean waves in frequency space, then reconstructs the surface with a 2D inverse FFT each step.",
      "Wind speed and direction drive the spectrum directly, while directional spread, damping, and choppiness shape crest sharpness and anisotropy."
    ]
  },
  "model": {
    "subtitle": "Directional spectral ocean simulation with phase evolution and GPU FFT reconstruction.",
    "references": [
      {
        "label": "dli/waves (WebGL ocean)",
        "url": "https://github.com/dli/waves"
      },
      {
        "label": "Tessendorf: Simulating Ocean Water",
        "url": "https://people.computing.clemson.edu/~jtessen/reports/papers_files/coursenotes2002.pdf"
      },
      {
        "label": "JONSWAP Wave Spectrum",
        "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/JONSWAP"
      }
    ],
    "items": [
      {
        "title": "Surface Reconstruction",
        "equation": "$$\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{k}_{n,m}&=2\\pi\\left(\\frac{n}{L_x},\\frac{m}{L_y}\\right),\\qquad n,m\\in[-N/2,N/2)\\\\\\eta(\\mathbf{x},t)&=\\operatorname{Re}\\sum_{n,m}\\hat{h}(\\mathbf{k}_{n,m},t)e^{i\\mathbf{k}_{n,m}\\cdot\\mathbf{x}}\\end{aligned}$$",
        "explanation": "The ocean surface is reconstructed from complex Fourier amplitudes on a periodic wave-number grid, then sampled by the rendered mesh.",
        "parameters": [
          "<strong>FFT Resolution</strong> (\\(N\\)) controls the number of frequency samples on each axis.",
          "<strong>World Sizes</strong> (\\(L_x,L_y\\)) set the physical domain and therefore the wave-number spacing.",
          "<strong>Mesh Resolution</strong> controls visible geometric tessellation."
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Complex Amplitude Evolution",
        "equation": "$$\\begin{aligned}\\phi_{\\mathbf{k}}(t+\\Delta t)&=\\left(\\phi_{\\mathbf{k}}(t)+\\omega(k)\\Delta t\\right)\\bmod 2\\pi\\\\\\hat{h}(\\mathbf{k},t)&=h_0(\\mathbf{k})e^{i\\phi_{\\mathbf{k}}(t)}+h_0^*(-\\mathbf{k})e^{-i\\phi_{\\mathbf{k}}(t)}\\end{aligned}$$",
        "explanation": "Each frequency advances by its dispersion phase each simulation step, while the conjugate pair keeps the reconstructed surface real-valued.",
        "parameters": [
          "<strong>Time Step</strong> (\\(\\Delta t\\)) controls phase advance per simulation update."
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Dispersion",
        "equation": "$$\\omega(k)=\\sqrt{gk\\left(1+\\left(\\frac{k}{k_m}\\right)^2\\right)},\\qquad k_p=g\\left(\\frac{\\Omega}{U_{10}}\\right)^2$$",
        "explanation": "The shader uses finite-depth-style capillary correction for angular frequency and a wind-coupled peak wave number for spectrum shaping.",
        "parameters": [
          "<strong>Wind Speed</strong> (\\(U_{10}\\)) shifts the dominant wave-number band through \\(k_p\\)."
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Directional Spectrum",
        "equation": "$$\\begin{aligned}\\tilde{S}(\\mathbf{k})&=A\\,E(U_{10})\\,S(k;U_{10})\\,D(\\theta-\\theta_w,\\sigma_\\theta)\\,e^{-d_s^2k^2}\\\\h_0(\\mathbf{k})&=\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{2}\\tilde{S}(\\mathbf{k})\\,\\Delta k_x\\Delta k_y}\\end{aligned}$$",
        "explanation": "Wind speed sets the energy scale and peak band, wind direction orients the directional lobe, and short-wave damping suppresses high-frequency ripples.",
        "parameters": [
          "<strong>Spectrum Scale</strong> (\\(A\\)) multiplies the wave energy.",
          "<strong>Wind Speed</strong> (\\(U_{10}\\)) sets \\(E(U_{10})\\) and the spectrum shape \\(S(k;U_{10})\\).",
          "<strong>Wind Direction</strong> (\\(\\theta_w\\)) aims the directional spectrum.",
          "<strong>Direction Spread</strong> (\\(\\sigma_\\theta\\)) controls the angular broadness of \\(D\\).",
          "<strong>Short-wave Damping</strong> (\\(d_s\\)) attenuates high wave numbers."
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Choppy Displacement",
        "equation": "$$\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{x}'&=\\mathbf{x}+s_d\\left(\\eta_x,\\eta_y,\\eta\\right),\\qquad (\\eta_x,\\eta_y)\\propto -i\\chi\\frac{\\mathbf{k}}{\\lVert\\mathbf{k}\\rVert}\\hat{h}(\\mathbf{k},t)\\\\\\mathbf{n}'&=\\operatorname{normalize}\\left((q_n n_x,\\,q_n n_y,\\,n_z)\\right)\\end{aligned}$$",
        "explanation": "Horizontal displacement is derived in frequency space from the wave direction, then scaled with the height field to sharpen crests. Normal strength only adjusts shading normals.",
        "parameters": [
          "<strong>Choppiness</strong> (\\(\\chi\\)) controls horizontal crest skew.",
          "<strong>Displacement Scale</strong> (\\(s_d\\)) scales the final surface displacement.",
          "<strong>Normal Strength</strong> (\\(q_n\\)) adjusts rendered shading normals without changing the simulated height field."
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
